<Layouts.flash_group flash={@flash} />

<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
  <.header>
    The design language
    <:subtitle>
      spec-10 Annex A, rendered. Every value comes from <code>priv/design</code>, generated into
      the stylesheet by <code>mix design.build</code>. Change one there and reload.
    </:subtitle>
    <:actions>
      <.button variant="bare" href={~p"/notices"}>Notices</.button>
    </:actions>
  </.header>

  <section aria-labelledby="contexts" class="mb-12">
    <h2 id="contexts" class="mb-1 text-title-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-strong">
      Contexts
    </h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
      A.1.6's five modifiers. Each writes two attributes on the document root — the resolved
      value and the intent — so <em>follow the system</em> is a state of its own. Theme resolves
      before contrast, which is why increased contrast picks a further step of whichever ramp
      the theme chose.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-4 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
      Four of the five are the person's and are kept with their principal, because §14.5 makes a
      contrast or motion setting disclose a disability and a household browser's storage is
      shared by everyone who uses it. <code>distance</code> is the exception: §4.4 records it with
      the device, so it stays in this browser and follows the screen rather than the person.
    </p>
    <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-raised p-4">
      <Layouts.context_controls contexts={@contexts} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="controls" class="mb-12">
    <h2 id="controls" class="mb-1 text-title-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-strong">
      Controls
    </h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
      A.11's emphasis ladder. <code>solid</code> is a field for a glyph, not for a label: no step
      of the ramp reaches 4.5:1 against its ink in both themes, so a control with a word in it is
      built from the subtle rung, where the surface's own ink reaches 13.71:1 and 14.41:1.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <.button variant="bare">Bare</.button>
      <.button variant="subtle">Subtle</.button>
      <.button variant="strong">Strong</.button>
      <.button variant="solid" aria-label="play">
        <.icon name="hero-play-mini" />
      </.button>
      <.button variant="subtle" disabled>Disabled</.button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="elevation" class="mb-12">
    <h2 id="elevation" class="mb-1 text-title-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-strong">
      Elevation
    </h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
      A.6: elevation is a step of surface tone, never a shadow, because on a dark surface a
      shadow darkens nothing. A tonal step measures 1.10:1 and cannot carry a boundary, so an
      edge that has to be perceived carries <code>border.strong</code> — the one role that clears
      3:1 against every surface in the ramp.
    </p>
    <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-base p-4">
      <p class="mb-3 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">surface.base</p>
      <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-raised p-4">
        <p class="mb-3 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">surface.raised</p>
        <div class="rounded-lg border-[length:var(--sys-border-width-component)] border-border-strong bg-surface-overlay p-4">
          <p class="text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
            surface.overlay, with a significant boundary
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="roles" class="mb-12">
    <h2 id="roles" class="mb-1 text-title-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-strong">
      Colour roles
    </h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
      The <code>sys</code> tier, which A.11 makes the public interface: adding a role is a minor
      change and renaming one is breaking. Every value here is a reference into the ramp, so a
      context that rebinds a primitive moves every role pointing at it.
    </p>

    <div :for={{group, roles} <- @roles} class="mb-6">
      <h3 class="mb-2 text-body-sm font-medium text-on-surface-muted">{group}</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <div
          :for={{name, variable} <- roles}
          class="overflow-hidden rounded-md border-[length:var(--sys-border-width-component)] border-border-subtle"
        >
          <div class="h-12" style={"background-color: var(#{variable})"}></div>
          <p class="bg-surface-raised px-2 py-1 text-caption text-on-surface-muted">{name}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ramp" class="mb-12">
    <h2 id="ramp" class="mb-1 text-title-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-strong">
      The neutral ramp
    </h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
      A.2.2's twelve steps, each with a written job, plus the focus ring — which is deliberately
      not a step, because no adjacent pair reaches 3:1 and a ring must clear it against every
      surface it can sit on. Templates bind to the roles above and never to these.
    </p>
    <div class="flex overflow-hidden rounded-md">
      <div :for={{step, variable} <- @ramp} class="grow">
        <div class="h-16" style={"background-color: var(#{variable})"}></div>
        <p class="bg-surface-raised py-1 text-center text-caption text-on-surface-muted">
          {step}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="type" class="mb-12">
    <h2 id="type" class="mb-1 text-title-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-strong">Type</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
      A.3.1's scale, every step in <code>rem</code>. A.3.2 holds the largest to at most 2.5 times
      the smallest, so <em>distance: far</em> moves one number — the root size — and the whole
      scale, the target floors, the radii and the focus width follow it.
    </p>
    <dl class="divide-y divide-border-subtle">
      <div :for={{name, variable, size} <- @scale} class="flex items-baseline gap-4 py-3">
        <dt class="w-32 shrink-0 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">{name}</dt>
        <dd class="w-16 shrink-0 text-caption text-on-surface-muted">{size}</dd>
        <dd
          class="truncate text-on-surface-strong"
          style={"font-size: var(#{variable}); line-height: var(#{String.replace(variable, "--sys-type-", "--sys-leading-")})"}
        >
          Peace of mind
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="status" class="mb-12">
    <h2 id="status" class="mb-1 text-title-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-strong">
      Status and class
    </h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
      A.2.6 spends saturation on two things only: the four status colours, and one hue per broad
      class. Five hues carry six classes because no sixth hue sits far enough from the others —
      the tightest existing pair is 134 rgb units apart and the best candidate fell to 95. Text
      and package share a hue for that reason.
    </p>
    <div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <span
        :for={status <- ~w(error warning success info)}
        class="rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-body-sm"
        style={"background-color: var(--sys-color-status-#{status}); color: var(--sys-color-on-status-#{status})"}
      >
        {status}
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <span
        :for={class <- ~w(video audio text image software package)}
        class="rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-body-sm"
        style={"background-color: var(--sys-color-class-#{class}); color: var(--sys-color-on-class)"}
      >
        {class}
      </span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="glyphs" class="mb-12">
    <h2 id="glyphs" class="mb-1 text-title-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-strong">
      The drawn glyphs
    </h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
      A.2.6 gives the glyph the job of identifying a category and colour the job of
      grouping by broad class, because colour is preattentive and poor at carrying many
      identities while a glyph survives monochrome, forced colours and three metres. These
      five are drawn because nothing in the base set's 324 serves them.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-6 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
      Each is shown at all three of A.8.2's grids — 16, 20 and 24 — at its own size and
      then enlarged, because the question A.8.5 asks is whether a reduction preserves the
      meaning and that is only answerable at the size it reduces to. The grids are separate
      drawings, not one scaled: repeats reduce in count, and a construction serving only a
      refinement is deleted rather than shrunk.
    </p>

    <div :for={{drawn, against, note} <- @glyphs} class="mb-6 rounded-lg bg-surface-raised p-4">
      <h3 class="text-body-md font-semibold text-on-surface-strong">{drawn}</h3>
      <p class="mt-1 mb-3 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">{note}</p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end gap-6">
        <div :for={{suffix, label} <- [{"-micro", "16"}, {"-mini", "20"}, {"", "24"}]}>
          <div class="flex items-end gap-3">
            <.icon name={drawn <> suffix} />
            <span class="text-on-surface-strong [&>svg]:size-12">
              <.icon name={drawn <> suffix} />
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1 text-caption text-on-surface-muted">{label}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div :if={against} class="mt-4 border-t border-border-subtle pt-3">
        <p class="mb-2 text-caption text-on-surface-muted">against {against}</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end gap-6">
          <div :for={{suffix, label} <- [{"-micro", "16"}, {"-mini", "20"}, {"", "24"}]}>
            <div class="flex items-end gap-3">
              <.icon name={against <> suffix} />
              <span class="text-on-surface-strong [&>svg]:size-12">
                <.icon name={against <> suffix} />
              </span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-1 text-caption text-on-surface-muted">{label}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="markers" class="mb-12">
    <h2 id="markers" class="mb-1 text-title-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-strong">
      The absence markers
    </h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
      One per state of §5.2 except <em>held</em>, which carries none — so a reader cannot
      tell a held value from one nobody computed, which is why <em>not yet examined</em> has
      a mark of its own and the state may never be left unset. Three channels carry the
      seven: a broken contour means no person established this, a knocked-out field means
      settled and will not change, and the interior mark separates what shares both.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-4">
      <div
        :for={{state, glyph, contour, field, mark} <- @markers}
        class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised p-3 text-center"
      >
        <div class="flex items-end justify-center gap-3">
          <.icon name={glyph} />
          <span class="text-on-surface-strong [&>svg]:size-12">
            <.icon name={glyph} />
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-caption text-on-surface-strong">{state}</p>
        <p class="text-caption text-on-surface-muted">{contour}, {field}, {mark}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="form" class="mb-12">
    <h2 id="form" class="mb-1 text-title-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-strong">
      Form primitives
    </h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
      Each at A.4.2's pointer floor, asked for by name rather than written as a number. The focus
      ring is drawn once in the stylesheet with <code>outline</code> and never a shadow, because a
      shadow computes to <code>none</code> under forced colours — so a shadow-only ring vanishes
      for exactly the people most likely to be in that mode. Tab through these to see it.
    </p>
    <div class="max-w-md rounded-lg bg-surface-raised p-4">
      <.input name="name" label="A field" value="A value" />
      <.input name="empty" label="An empty field" value="" placeholder="Nothing here yet" />
      <.input name="broken" label="A field in error" value="Not a year" errors={["is invalid"]} />
      <.input
        name="pick"
        type="select"
        label="A choice"
        value="two"
        options={[{"One", "one"}, {"Two", "two"}]}
      />
      <.input name="agree" type="checkbox" label="A checkbox" value={true} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="data" class="mb-12">
    <h2 id="data" class="mb-1 text-title-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-strong">
      Lists and tables
    </h2>
    <div class="mb-6 rounded-lg bg-surface-raised p-4">
      <.list>
        <:item title="Name">Kind of Blue</:item>
        <:item title="Released">1959</:item>
        <:item title="Language">
          <span class="text-on-surface-muted">not yet examined</span>
        </:item>
      </.list>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-raised p-4">
      <.table
        id="demo"
        rows={[%{step: "09", job: "solid background"}, %{step: "12", job: "high-contrast text"}]}
      >
        <:col :let={row} label="Step">{row.step}</:col>
        <:col :let={row} label="Job">{row.job}</:col>
      </.table>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
